# Testing

## Writing E2E Tests

- MUST prefer getByRole, getByText, getByTestId selectors in playwright to closely mimic how a user will identify
  elements.
- MUST NOT use .locator unless absolutely necessary and MUST provide a comment justifying the need
- SHOULD use .serial for running test when each test case depend on the previous one in the cases where you are testing
  long user flows
- SHOULD re-use existing auth storage state during tests that require a logged in user
- SHOULD re-use existing test-only api endpoints to make tests more reliable
- COULD create test-only api endpoints to allow clean CRUD of test related data

This repo: specs live in `e2e/`. Chair product still has **no** `/api/patients` CRUD (Dexie + supabase-js). Seed **fake** patients only. Do not add test endpoints that skip RLS or use the service role.

## Debugging E2E Tests

When dealing with e2e test failures, you should make use of the detailed test results generated by playwright at test-results. For each test failure, you will be given the playwright output, where you can find the error context md and the end state screenshot, use that to help you fix the failures.

